# Simulation-model correction (user ruling 2026-09-29, METHODOLOGY "Roll rate gains").
# The iris SITL airframe has 2.25x the roll authority per inertia of pitch (full-body
# Ixx 0.01252 vs Iyy 0.01743 kg m^2 incl. rotor masses; rotor arms 0.210 m roll vs 0.130 m
# pitch: (0.210/0.01252)/(0.130/0.01743) = 2.249) but ran IDENTICAL firmware-default rate
# gains on both axes (P 0.135, I 0.135, D 0.0036), giving a 17.5 Hz roll rate-loop limit
# cycle (0.40 rad/s rms, motors +-67 us). Roll P/I/D are scaled by 1/2.249 = 0.4447 so the
# roll loop gain matches the (stable) pitch loop. Pitch, yaw, filters, FF, angle loops unchanged.
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.06003
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.06003
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.0016
